From 2323052b02e23cd26673776f69ff900d12caca68 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hank Yeomans <hank@quorra.ah.local>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 00:04:04 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 32/60] moe: persistent FlashInfer CUTLASS MXFP4 workspace per
 device (E34d-v (i))

FlashInfer's cutlass_fused_moe allocated and freed a ~980 MiB scratch on every
call; across long prefills that churn fragmented the caching allocator until no
contiguous block was left (1M x 1 died at ~306K prefix, 262K x 4 at ~190K, with
>1.8 GiB reserved-but-free). fused_experts_none_to_flashinfer_mxfp4 now passes
one buffer per device sized by cutlass_fused_moe_workspace_size for the
prefill-chunk ceiling (max_prefill_buffer_tokens / max_running_requests, or
SGLANG_FLASHINFER_MOE_WORKSPACE_MAX_ROWS), allocated at the first (pre-capture)
call and never resized. Larger forwards or non-fitting configurations fall back
to per-call allocation with one warning; allocation inside graph capture is
refused. SGLANG_FLASHINFER_MOE_PERSISTENT_WORKSPACE=0 restores the old path.

Amp-Thread-ID: https://ampcode.com/threads/T-01a0c10b-a5f8-77fc-b238-7147d12ccf29
Co-authored-by: Amp <amp@ampcode.com>
